is  a  One  Time Password (OTP) authentication system.  It is in‐
tended to be used when the communication channel between  a  user
and  host is not secure (e.g. not encrypted or hardwired).  Since
each password is used only once, even if it is "seen" by  a  hos‐
tile  third  party, it cannot be used again to gain access to the
host.  uses 64 bits of information, transformed by the  algorithm
into  6  English words.  The user supplies the words to authenti‐
cate himself to programs like or Example use  of  the  program  %
skey   99   th91334  Enter password: <your secret password is en‐
tered here> OMEN US HORN OMIT BACK AHOY  %  The  string  that  is
given  back  by  can then be used to log into a system.  The pro‐
grams that are part of the system are: used to set up  your  used
